WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.634
-Timothée Chalamet.

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:02.802
Always good to see you, buddy.

00:00:02.802 --> 00:00:04.237
Thank you so much
for coming back to our show.

00:00:04.237 --> 00:00:06.039
-Thanks for having me back.
-You got such a great energy.

00:00:06.039 --> 00:00:07.206
Every time I run into you,
you're always --

00:00:07.206 --> 00:00:08.741
-And you were surprised
backstage, right?

00:00:08.741 --> 00:00:10.409
-Yeah, I was.
-I scared Jimmy backstage.

00:00:10.409 --> 00:00:12.044
Because he knocked on my door,
I went "Aaaah!"

00:00:12.044 --> 00:00:14.146
[ Laughter ]
-You were right behind the door.

00:00:14.146 --> 00:00:15.948
Normally, I knock on the door,
and then, open it up

00:00:15.948 --> 00:00:18.017
and walk into the dressing room.
I opened up, but you --

00:00:18.017 --> 00:00:19.719
you were right there
and jumped out at me, yeah.

00:00:19.719 --> 00:00:21.087
-I had been waiting.
I was there.

00:00:21.087 --> 00:00:22.422
-I wanted --
How long were you waiting for?

00:00:22.422 --> 00:00:23.656
-For three hours.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:23.656 --> 00:00:25.959
-I want to ask you
about this photo here,

00:00:25.959 --> 00:00:28.962
because we've had Kim Kardashian
on the show and Pete Davidson,

00:00:28.962 --> 00:00:30.596
and they were
talking about this night.

00:00:30.596 --> 00:00:32.698
There's a picture of you guys

00:00:32.698 --> 00:00:35.401
out to dinner with Kid Cudi
and Kanye West.

00:00:35.401 --> 00:00:38.304
-Okay. So, Kid Cudi
is my favorite artist ever.

00:00:38.304 --> 00:00:39.439
I wouldn't be acting
without him.

00:00:39.439 --> 00:00:41.140
I wouldn't pursue
this crazy career,

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:42.575
and I just text him one morning,
his birthday, and he said,

00:00:42.575 --> 00:00:43.776
"Oh, come to dinner tonight."

00:00:43.776 --> 00:00:45.445
I did not know that was
what I was walking into.

00:00:45.445 --> 00:00:47.446
Which was awesome
but was surreal.

00:00:47.446 --> 00:00:49.182
Had to go in the bathroom,
send a couple of texts,

00:00:49.182 --> 00:00:50.816
like, you know...
[ Laughter ]

00:00:50.816 --> 00:00:52.919
-So, you thought you were
going to dinner with Kid Cudi.

00:00:52.919 --> 00:00:54.920
-Yeah, which would've
already been very surreal.

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:56.723
Because that's a --
You know, whenever I'm, like,

00:00:56.723 --> 00:00:58.057
trying to have a good time,

00:00:58.057 --> 00:01:00.159
but I'm also, like, coming off
weird, like right now.

00:01:00.159 --> 00:01:01.928
-No, no, no, no, no.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:01.928 --> 00:01:03.562
You're coming off
totally normal and fun.

00:01:03.562 --> 00:01:05.364
So, you get there
and Pete Davidson's there.

00:01:05.364 --> 00:01:06.665
Do you know Pete?
-Yeah, Pete's great.

00:01:06.665 --> 00:01:07.900
He's a fellow New Yorker.

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:10.836
Just did a movie
with my sister, actually."

00:01:10.836 --> 00:01:12.305
-Oh, really?
-Yeah, Judd Apatow movie.

00:01:12.305 --> 00:01:13.506
-No way.
-Yes.

00:01:13.506 --> 00:01:16.108
-So, it's you,
Pete, and Kid Cudi.

00:01:16.108 --> 00:01:18.010
And then, how do you know
if Kim and Kanye are coming?

00:01:18.010 --> 00:01:19.679
-Well, I got there,
and I had sneaking suspicion,

00:01:19.679 --> 00:01:21.781
but they weren't -- there was
not enough seats for everyone,

00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:23.115
so I thought
I was gonna be safe.

00:01:23.115 --> 00:01:25.151
And then --
Not safe, but it was.

00:01:25.151 --> 00:01:26.652
[ Laughter ]

00:01:26.652 --> 00:01:28.320
And then, we're hanging out,
and then it feels like

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:29.522
there's an earthquake
in the restaurant,

00:01:29.522 --> 00:01:32.225
but it was -- it was --
it was, like, epic.

00:01:32.225 --> 00:01:33.626
You know, you can feel the,
like --

00:01:33.626 --> 00:01:34.827
-The energy shift.

00:01:34.827 --> 00:01:36.662
-You turn around,
and I was like, "Holy [bleep]"

00:01:36.662 --> 00:01:37.830
You know, 'cause, like,

00:01:37.830 --> 00:01:39.832
I feel like I'm in this now
a little bit.

00:01:39.832 --> 00:01:43.102
But then, I'm like, "I can't --
I can't feel, like --

00:01:43.102 --> 00:01:44.904
I feel like too much
of a fraud or something."

00:01:44.904 --> 00:01:46.839
So, I'm like,
"What?! This is nuts." Yeah.

00:01:46.839 --> 00:01:48.741
-That you were sitting with
Kid Cudi and Kanye?

00:01:48.741 --> 00:01:50.810
Or Kim or what?
-All of them, man.

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:52.512
I'm not -- I'm not --
-And where was this? What room?

00:01:52.512 --> 00:01:53.712
-Well, that's in a back room
at that point.

00:01:53.712 --> 00:01:55.014
You know,
I went to the bathroom.

00:01:55.014 --> 00:01:56.782
Seriously, I sent a text
to two friends, and my words,

00:01:56.782 --> 00:01:58.685
like, "Does this make sense?"

00:01:58.685 --> 00:02:00.419
And they were like,
"Man, 16-year-old you

00:02:00.419 --> 00:02:01.454
would slap the [bleep]
out of you.

00:02:01.454 --> 00:02:03.556
Go back to the table."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:03.556 --> 00:02:05.458
And I went to the table,
and then, like --

00:02:05.458 --> 00:02:06.793
And then, it was fun.
It was a good time.

00:02:06.793 --> 00:02:07.927
And then, you have enough, like,

00:02:07.927 --> 00:02:09.161
random whatever
they have on the table,

00:02:09.161 --> 00:02:10.463
and then you forget about
all of it, anyway.

00:02:10.463 --> 00:02:13.333
-Yeah, exactly.
It's fun, yeah.

00:02:13.333 --> 00:02:14.834
-Now don't do that.
It's not a healthy way

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:16.235
to deal with it,
but in that moment, yeah.

00:02:16.235 --> 00:02:18.437
[ Laughter ]
-With 16-year-old you,

00:02:18.437 --> 00:02:22.474
what would you be doing,
if not acting?

00:02:22.474 --> 00:02:23.776
-I'm not good at anything else.

00:02:23.776 --> 00:02:25.111
That's the only thing
I'm, like, decent at.

00:02:25.111 --> 00:02:26.545
I mean, like, my mom's
a dance teacher,

00:02:26.545 --> 00:02:27.580
so maybe something in the arts,

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:28.981
maybe, like,
dancing or something.

00:02:28.981 --> 00:02:32.684
-'Cause I do have a photo of you
in a dance -- a dance thing.

00:02:32.684 --> 00:02:34.787
It's pretty awesome.
-That's --

00:02:34.787 --> 00:02:37.023
This is you at
the National Dance Institute.

00:02:37.023 --> 00:02:39.658
This is you as Cupid.
[ Audience "Awws" ]

00:02:39.658 --> 00:02:41.927
I mean,
I think you have a future.

00:02:41.927 --> 00:02:46.365
Timothée.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:46.365 --> 00:02:48.734
Come on!
How cute is that?

00:02:48.734 --> 00:02:50.403
You got good form, buddy.

00:02:50.403 --> 00:02:51.971
What do you remember about this?

00:02:51.971 --> 00:02:53.506
-I remember absolutely nothing.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:53.506 --> 00:02:55.108
-Come on!
-That's not even me!

00:02:55.108 --> 00:02:56.376
-Come on. Come on.

00:02:56.376 --> 00:02:59.645
No, it's not even you.
Just a random kid, yeah.

00:02:59.645 --> 00:03:00.813
-They just brought that up.
No, that was surreal.

00:03:00.813 --> 00:03:02.147
That's actually
at my high school

00:03:02.147 --> 00:03:03.582
that I went to, eventually,
so the first time I was

00:03:03.582 --> 00:03:05.118
on that stage was at
the high school I went to.

00:03:05.118 --> 00:03:06.185
And nobody
would care about that,

00:03:06.185 --> 00:03:07.586
but that's something I remember.

00:03:07.586 --> 00:03:09.689
-No, people do care about that.

00:03:09.689 --> 00:03:12.225
I saw somewhere,
we were reading up on you,

00:03:12.225 --> 00:03:14.727
and it said on your résumé,
your acting résumé,

00:03:14.727 --> 00:03:16.896
you put things on there like --
besides acting --

00:03:16.896 --> 00:03:18.698
skills that you could do.
-Yes.

00:03:18.698 --> 00:03:20.667
-One of them, I think,
was dance.

00:03:20.667 --> 00:03:22.735
Maybe one of them was chess,
I want to say?

00:03:22.735 --> 00:03:24.437
-It was random.
My mom used to fill out

00:03:24.437 --> 00:03:25.838
my résumé,
so they have special skills,

00:03:25.838 --> 00:03:27.874
and you go in for auditions.
-Chess. [ Laughs ]

00:03:27.874 --> 00:03:29.542
-Like, no casting director's
gonna be like,

00:03:29.542 --> 00:03:31.277
"This kid plays chess!
Let's put him in a movie."

00:03:31.277 --> 00:03:32.845
[ Laughter ]
-"Can you fake chess?"

00:03:32.845 --> 00:03:35.381
-But it was a lot.
It was like, chess, bike riding,

00:03:35.381 --> 00:03:37.149
you know, swimming.
Like normal [bleep]

00:03:37.149 --> 00:03:38.351
Normal things.
Sorry, sorry.

00:03:38.351 --> 00:03:41.054
-You can't say that word.
-Sorry, sorry, sorry.

00:03:41.054 --> 00:03:43.155
-Do you know how much money
you're costing NBC right now?

00:03:43.155 --> 00:03:45.391
Oh, my God.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:46.826
It's gonna hurt
the opening weekend.

00:03:46.826 --> 00:03:48.027
Trust me, buddy.
-No!

00:03:48.027 --> 00:03:50.729
-No, no.
But we saw that on there.

00:03:50.729 --> 00:03:52.631
And one of the things
that's on there was juggling.

00:03:52.631 --> 00:03:54.300
-Juggling, yeah.
I used to be able to know --

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:55.434
Well, maybe, I --

00:03:55.434 --> 00:03:56.969
But you have juggling balls
right here?

00:03:56.969 --> 00:04:00.340
[ Cheers and applause ]
-I'm just saying...

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:03.075
Now, I don't know anything.
I can't do --

00:04:03.075 --> 00:04:04.811
I can't do it at all.

00:04:04.811 --> 00:04:06.579
I'm terrible.
I really have no clue.

00:04:06.579 --> 00:04:08.081
Can you juggle?
-Let's take a shot. Okay.

00:04:08.081 --> 00:04:10.283
-Yeah, it's Timothée Chalamet
juggling.

00:04:10.283 --> 00:04:12.819
Giving it a shot.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:12.819 --> 00:04:14.987
-All right.

00:04:14.987 --> 00:04:16.822
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:16.822 --> 00:04:19.725
-Come on, bud!
Come on, dude.

00:04:19.725 --> 00:04:21.126
You already had your spot.

00:04:21.126 --> 00:04:22.828
It's like a talent show here.
-Like a talent show.

00:04:22.828 --> 00:04:23.963
-It's like a talent show.

00:04:23.963 --> 00:04:26.499
-What would your juggling
equivalent be?

00:04:26.499 --> 00:04:27.633
-What, do I just?

00:04:27.633 --> 00:04:29.168
-Like special skill,
weird, random thing.

00:04:29.168 --> 00:04:30.302
-Oh, I have the worst special --

00:04:30.302 --> 00:04:32.571
I don't know
what my special skills was.

00:04:32.571 --> 00:04:35.941
My special skill was --
I guess I do impressions.

00:04:35.941 --> 00:04:37.443
That was my --
-Well, dude, you're the host --

00:04:37.443 --> 00:04:39.646
This is amazing.
-I know, but if I'm gonna be

00:04:39.646 --> 00:04:40.846
in a movie,
you don't need somebody

00:04:40.846 --> 00:04:42.681
who's gonna do impressions.
-"Fever Pitch."

00:04:42.681 --> 00:04:43.816
Who's seen "Fever Pitch" here?

00:04:43.816 --> 00:04:45.818
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:45.818 --> 00:04:47.253
Yes, no.
-Stop it!

00:04:47.253 --> 00:04:48.421
-No, I'm not gonna
get into anything.

